  "Alaska is the northernmost, westernmost and, because its Aleutian Islands cross the 180th meridian, also the easternmost US state.",
  "Reno, Nevada, lies farther west than Los Angeles, California.",
  "Just across the river from Detroit, the Canadian city of Windsor lies to the south of it, not the north.",
  "Because of the way Panama twists, the Pacific entrance of the Panama Canal is east of its Atlantic entrance.",
  "Bull sharks swim up the San Juan River into Lake Nicaragua and live in its fresh water.",
  "Lake Superior holds enough water to cover all of North and South America about 30 cm deep.",
  "Finland has around 188,000 lakes, about one for every 30 people.",
  "The village of Oymyakon in Siberia once recorded about -68°C, and people live there year-round.",
  "Russia's Vostok research station in Antarctica recorded -89.2°C in 1983, the coldest temperature ever measured by a ground weather station.",
  "Satellites have measured the ground in Iran's Lut Desert at over 70°C, among the hottest surfaces on Earth.",
  "Sweden has about 267,000 islands, more than any other country.",
