  "The Congo is the deepest river in the world, plunging to over 220 m in places.",
  "The Congo River crosses the equator twice on its way to the sea.",
  "The Danube flows through or along 10 countries, more than any other river.",
  "Saudi Arabia, one of the world's largest countries, has no permanent rivers at all.",
  "Ulaanbaatar in Mongolia is the coldest national capital in the world by average yearly temperature.",
  "La Paz, Bolivia's seat of government, sits at about 3,600 m, the highest of any such city in the world.",
  "Reykjavík is the northernmost capital of a sovereign country, and Wellington is the southernmost.",
