  "Australia's Lord Howe Island lets only about 400 tourists stay at any one time.",
  "The Pitcairn Islands in the Pacific have only around 50 residents.",
  "For decades the main road into Gibraltar crossed straight over the airport runway, and traffic stopped whenever a plane landed. A tunnel beneath it finally opened in 2023.",
  "Kinshasa and Brazzaville face each other across the Congo River, the closest pair of capitals apart from Rome and Vatican City.",
  "Lake Malawi is home to more fish species than any other lake on Earth, most of them colourful cichlids.",
  "Lake Baikal has its own seal, the nerpa, one of the very few seals that live only in fresh water.",
  "Brazil borders every country in South America except Chile and Ecuador.",
  "Bolivia is landlocked but still has a navy, which patrols Lake Titicaca and the country's rivers.",
  "Spain sits mostly west of Greenwich, yet it runs on Central European Time, an hour ahead of what the sun suggests.",
  "The equator passes through 13 countries, from Ecuador to Kiribati.",
  "Argentina is named after silver (argentum in Latin), and Venezuela's name means 'little Venice'.",
  "Canada's name likely comes from kanata, an Iroquoian word meaning 'village' or 'settlement'.",
  "Zealandia is a hidden continent around New Zealand, with roughly 94% of it under the sea.",
  "Iceland straddles two tectonic plates that are pulling apart, so the country grows about 2 cm wider every year.",
