  "Europe's first banknotes were issued in 1661 by a Swedish bank, Stockholms Banco, partly because Sweden's copper coins were so huge and heavy.",
  "On the island of Yap, giant stone discs up to about 3.6 meters wide served as money. Ownership could change hands without the stone ever moving.",
  "Some of the world's first coins were minted in ancient Lydia, around 600 BCE, from electrum, a natural mix of gold and silver.",
  "The first cash machine opened in London in 1967. Its inventor wanted a 6-digit PIN, but settled on 4 because his wife said that was all she could remember.",
