  "The first spam email was sent in 1978 to a few hundred users of ARPANET, the internet's ancestor, advertising new computers.",
  "The oldest surviving photograph from nature, taken in France around 1827, needed an exposure of at least several hours.",
  "The first traffic light was installed outside the Houses of Parliament in London in 1868. It was gas-lit and operated by hand by a police officer.",
  "Rubber got its English name in 1770, when scientist Joseph Priestley noticed it was great for rubbing out pencil marks.",
