  "The ballpoint pen was patented in 1938 by Hungarian journalist László Bíró, which is why the British still call any ballpoint pen a 'biro'.",
  "Correction fluid was invented by a secretary, Bette Nesmith Graham, in her kitchen. She later sold the company for $47.5 million.",
  "The safety pin was invented in 1849 by Walter Hunt, who sold the patent for just $400 to pay off a small debt.",
